=== in operator emits pythonic form
if (xs.contains(2))

=== not in operator
if (!xs.contains(2))

=== boolean operators
System.out.println(String.valueOf(a && b))

=== bitwise operators
int y = x & 15

=== compound assignment operators
x += 5

=== chained comparison
return 0 <= x && x <= 255

=== truthiness check on list
if (xs.size() > 0)

=== truthiness check on string
if (!s.isEmpty())
